<!-- ============ THE LEAK — sticky section ============ -->
<section id="leaks">
  <div class="wrap sticky-sec">
    <div class="sticky-left">
      <div class="kicker">The leak</div>
      <h2 class="h2">Where the money<br>actually goes</h2>
      <p class="lead">You don't have a marketing problem. You have a <b>catching problem</b> — the calls, clicks and customers already coming at you are falling through.</p>
      <div class="sdots" id="sdots"><i class="on"></i><i></i><i></i></div>
    </div>
    <div id="leakcards">
      <div class="leak-card rv">
        <div class="n">LEAK 01</div>
        <h3>Missed calls</h3>
        <p>62% of calls to small businesses go unanswered. After hours, it's nearly all of them — and 85% of missed callers never call back. They call the next result on Google.</p>
        <div class="stat">$1,200+<small> /mo walking away</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="leak-card rv">
        <div class="n">LEAK 02</div>
        <h3>A website that doesn't sell</h3>
        <p>If your site takes 6 seconds to load, isn't mobile-first, or buries the phone number — visitors bounce to a competitor whose site does the job.</p>
        <div class="stat">53%<small> bounce on slow mobile sites</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="leak-card rv">
        <div class="n">LEAK 03</div>
        <h3>Silent reviews</h3>
        <p>Buyers read reviews before they call. If you're not asking every happy customer for one — and answering the bad ones — your rating is set by your angriest 2%.</p>
        <div class="stat">88%<small> trust reviews like referrals</small></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ LEAK, ADDED UP: dark animated beat ============ -->
